  "result": "Copying it avoids the cross-module dependency, but for something like currency formatting \u2014 where a rounding/locale bug fix needs to land everywhere at once \u2014 silent drift between two copies is the worse failure mode than either team depending on a neutral shared location.\n\nI'd put it in a top-level `shared/` (or `common/`) directory that neither `reports/` nor `billing/` owns, so both import from a shared utility rather than from each other's folder \u2014 that's a much smaller coupling cost than duplicating financial-formatting logic. If your build supports it, you could even make `shared/` its own small internal package with a version, so either team can bump it independently when they need to tweak behavior.\n\nWant me to go ahead and set up a `shared/` folder and move `formatCurrency.js` there with imports updated in both modules?",
